  "prompt_text": "Use reference 1 only as simple silhouette/camera diagram; reference 2 is a verified approved same-kit geometry/view guide; reference 3 is the exact target source contact and controls all stone materials, banners, metal rings and identity. Generate one transparent pixel-art atlas with TWO rows (outer corner first, inner corner second) and FOUR equal cells per row, columns FRONT, RIGHT, LEFT, REAR. These four are true level 90-degree elevations with vertical axis world Z, and all four show a broad rectangular joined wall face at the same total height; no isometric corners, no L silhouette, no standalone narrow post, no visible top surface. The physical object is a compact L-footprint corner of two perpendicular joined stone wings. From each camera, show the face-on branch as a broad rectangular elevation and only the physically visible narrow end of the perpendicular branch; maintain consistent dimensions and corner orientation across opposite directions. Use exactly the number and placement of source banners per row: outer source has one red hanging banner and one bronze ring detail; inner has two red hanging banners. Retain blue-gray masonry blocks, pale sandstone cap blocks and dark mortar/iron outline from the target source. Hidden faces inferred conservatively. No extra props, no letters, no shadows beyond the sprite, no cell spill. Crisp orthographic pixel art, transparent background.",
